{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2136-11-12 01:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. You're in the emergency department. You came in because of confusion and low blood pressure. We’re going to help you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2136-11-12 01:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2136-11-12 01:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know you can’t speak, but I’ll explain what’s happening. Your potassium level is very high, which can affect your heart. We’ve given you medicine to bring it down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2136-11-12 01:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2136-11-12 01:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your EKG showed changes from high potassium. We also started antibiotics because we think you have pneumonia and a possible urinary infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2136-11-12 01:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2136-11-12 01:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We replaced your Foley catheter and it drained nearly 2 liters. That means it was blocked. This likely caused kidney stress and part of your illness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2136-11-12 01:56:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2136-11-12 02:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re being admitted to the ICU for close monitoring. We’ll keep treating the infection and support your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2136-11-12 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your potassium is better now—down to 5.9. Your mental status is improving. You’re responding to questions with nods."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2136-11-12 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2136-11-12 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray shows pneumonia, likely from aspiration. We’ve started two antibiotics—cefepime and linezolid—to cover the bacteria we suspect."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2136-11-12 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2136-11-12 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also found Proteus mirabilis in your sputum. It’s sensitive to cefepime, so we’ll continue that. Linezolid may be stopped later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2136-11-12 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re giving your first dose of IV antibiotics on the floor. You’ve been moved from ICU because you’re more stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2136-11-12 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2136-11-12 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine was high at 2.6 but is now improving. Your kidneys are recovering after the catheter was replaced."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2136-11-12 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2136-11-12 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re watching your calcium and phosphate—they’re low. We’ve started vitamin D and will give supplements."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2136-11-13 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your white blood cell count is coming down—from 25.8 to 18. That means the antibiotics are working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2136-11-13 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2136-11-13 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your breathing is better. Lungs are clearer. We’ll keep the antibiotics going for a full 8-day course as recommended by infectious disease."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2136-11-13 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your feeding tube nutrition is running smoothly. We cleared a clog yesterday with a flush."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2136-11-13 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2136-11-14 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We spoke with your son. He confirmed you’re able to make decisions. You refused a PICC line for antibiotics at home, which is okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2136-11-14 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2136-11-14 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "So instead, you’ll stay here to finish all 8 days of IV antibiotics. That means discharge will be delayed by a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2136-11-14 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2136-11-14 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR was high at first—3.4—so we held your warfarin. Now it’s low, under 2, so we’ve started enoxaparin injections to prevent clots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2136-11-14 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2136-11-14 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re increasing your warfarin dose to 5 mg daily. Once your INR is stable, you can stop the injections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2136-11-15 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We placed a midline for IV access. It’s easier than a PICC and will last through your antibiotic course."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2136-11-15 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2136-11-15 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The midline was placed successfully. You’re doing well with it—no pain or swelling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2136-11-15 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2136-11-16 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your fentanyl patch is back on. We held it at first because of confusion, but now it’s safe to restart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2136-11-16 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2136-11-16 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also increased your oral morphine for pain from your pressure ulcers. You’ve been taking up to 15 mg a few times a day without issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2136-11-16 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2136-11-16 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Palliative care visited. They suggest keeping your current pain plan and considering methadone later. For now, we’ll stick with what’s working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2136-11-16 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2136-11-17 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your blood cultures came back negative. No bloodstream infection. Urine culture showed yeast, but we won’t treat it unless you have symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2136-11-17 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2136-11-17 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your kidney function is excellent now—creatinine is 0.2. Your electrolytes are stabilizing with supplements."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2136-11-17 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2136-11-17 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your Foley catheter kinked yesterday, causing discomfort. The nurses flushed it and it’s working fine. We couldn’t upsize it, so we’ll teach your nursing home team to flush it if flow drops."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2136-11-17 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2136-11-18 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re nearing the end of your antibiotic course. One more day of IV cefepime, then you’ll be ready for discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2136-11-18 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2136-11-18 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll send instructions to your nursing home: continue warfarin at 5 mg, give enoxaparin twice daily until INR is stable, and start daily vitamin D."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2136-11-18 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2136-11-18 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, increase morphine to 15 mg every 4 hours as needed. And flush the Foley if output slows—use 100 cc saline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2136-11-19 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final day of IV antibiotics. You’ve completed the full 8-day course. Your lungs are clear, and labs are normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2136-11-19 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2136-11-19 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll remove the midline today. You’re ready to go back to the nursing home tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2136-11-19 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2136-11-19 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your son confirmed he doesn’t want hospice discussed, but palliative care will help with pain management at the facility."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2136-11-19 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re being discharged today to extended care. You’ve recovered well from pneumonia and kidney injury."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Remember: take warfarin daily, use enoxaparin until INR is checked, take vitamin D, and use morphine for pain. Flush the Foley if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your code status remains DNR/DNI, as discussed with your family. We’ll follow up with your care team to ensure smooth transition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great. Stay hydrated, and your nursing home will monitor for any signs of infection or breathing issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll check your vitamin D levels soon and adjust if needed. Otherwise, keep up with your routine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Any questions? Just nod if you’re okay with everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Alright. The transport team will take you shortly. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll call your facility to confirm they received all instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You responded well to treatment. The main concerns were pneumonia, high potassium, and kidney injury—all resolved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your pain is better controlled now with increased morphine. We’ll keep monitoring through your care team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just rest now. You’re on the mend."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re proud of your progress. See you soon for follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll make sure your team knows everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2136-11-20 08:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set for discharge. Rest well."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2136-11-12 01:45:00",
    "admission_end": "2136-11-20 16:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 68-year-old male with a history of quadriplegia, tracheostomy, GJ tube, and chronic Foley catheter was admitted from his nursing home for altered mental status and hypotension. He was found to have hyperkalemia with peaked T waves, acute kidney injury likely due to obstructive uropathy, and hospital-acquired and aspiration pneumonia. He received emergency treatment for hyperkalemia and was started on IV cefepime and linezolid. His Foley catheter was replaced, draining 1.8 liters, and his renal function improved. Sputum culture grew Proteus mirabilis, sensitive to cefepime. Infectious disease recommended completing 8 days of cefepime. The patient refused a PICC line, so he remained hospitalized to complete IV therapy. His warfarin was held due to elevated INR, then restarted at 5 mg daily with bridging enoxaparin due to subtherapeutic levels. Chronic pain from pressure ulcers was managed with increased PRN morphine and palliative care consultation. He was discharged to extended care with instructions to continue antibiotics orally, manage pain, monitor INR, and follow up on electrolytes and vitamin D.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified septicemia",
      "Pneumonitis due to inhalation of food or vomitus",
      "Pneumonia due to other gram-negative bacteria",
      "Quadriplegia, unspecified",
      "Pressure ulcer, stage IV",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Delirium due to conditions classified elsewhere",
      "Hyperpotassemia",
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Disorders of magnesium metabolism",
      "Severe sepsis",
      "Tracheostomy status",
      "Other gastrostomy complications",
      "Urinary obstruction, unspecified",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Leukocytosis, unspecified",
      "Unspecified vitamin D deficiency",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Do not resuscitate status",
      "Ileostomy status",
      "Personal history, urinary (tract) infection",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants"
    ]
  }
}
